            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "8.3 What are the different States of Water?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.082,
            0.898,
            0.118,
            0.914
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "150"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.182,
            0.885,
            0.306
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Water is a substance that can be observed in three different states in our daily life. In the solid state, it exists as ice. On heating, the ice melts and gets converted into its liquid state. On further heating, water gets converted into its gaseous state. Let us perform Activity 8.5 to identify the properties of different states of water."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.317,
            0.549,
            0.339
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 8.5: Let us identify"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.35,
            0.885,
            0.433
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Put an ice cube in one container and transfer it to another container of different shape. What changes do you notice in the shape of the ice cube? Record your observations in Table 8.3."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.438,
            0.885,
            0.541
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Pour water from one container to another container of a different shape. Observe how water behaves compared to the ice cube and make a record. Did you notice how water flows from one container to the other? What happens to its shape?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.545,
            0.883,
            0.587
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Pour water on a clean surface and observe how it spreads."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.592,
            0.884,
            0.654
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " When water gets converted into water vapour, how does this water vapour spread? Compare this with the spreading behaviour of water."
            }
          ]
        },
